public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T00:44:48Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T00:44:48Z","body":"I found an old custom template on my hard drive and tried it with Godot 4.4.1, but even then the buttons/triggers were swapped. And when released, they remained pressed at 0.5. That's what the `+` configuration was for. \r\n\r\nI think back then I always pressed both triggers simultaneously during testing and didn't notice that they were swapped  😃 \r\n\r\n```\r\nGodot Engine v4.3.beta.custom_build.7fea02856 (2024-06-06 15:14:24 UTC) - https://godotengine.org\r\nOpenGL API OpenGL ES 3.2 V@0502.0 (GIT@193b2ee, I593c16c433, 1633593732) (Date:10/07/21) - Compatibility - Using Device: Qualcomm - Adreno (TM) 650\r\n\r\n+ Found newly connected joypad #0: Xbox One Controller - 58626f7820576972656c65737320436f\r\n```\r\n\r\n<img width=\"501\" height=\"303\" alt=\"Bildschirmfoto 2026-02-12 um 01 38 54\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6f0161ff-7fa6-4b72-9620-279d921fb8c7\" />\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3888029177/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3888618703","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114338#issuecomment-3888618703","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114338","id":3888618703,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nx5zP","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T04:26:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T04:41:54Z","body":"Ohh I see, thank you for testing! :D\nI will see if I'm able to reproduce it with my Xbox controller too and I will see what I can do, maybe I will have to port more code from SDL.\n\nEDIT: The triggers are not swapped on my controller, but they are mapped to [-1;1], this will also need to be fixed without breaking my Dualshock 4 triggers","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3888618703/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3888940211","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114338#issuecomment-3888940211","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114338","id":3888940211,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nzISz","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T06:33:39Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T07:53:33Z","body":"So I found some differences between how Godot handles Android joypad axes and how SDL handles them.\r\nGodot checks for duplicate axes:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/40448082abe972daa179c64d7889cd88a8e7ea9c/platform/android/java/lib/src/main/java/org/godotengine/godot/input/GodotInputHandler.java#L389-L407\r\n\r\nSDL does not:\r\nhttps://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/blob/4e2fd57e77fb4a28c0eeef0670fc4121cc2cf1f9/android-project/app/src/main/java/org/libsdl/app/SDLControllerManager.java#L230-L240\r\n```java\r\n                    List<InputDevice.MotionRange> ranges = joystickDevice.getMotionRanges();\r\n                    Collections.sort(ranges, new RangeComparator());\r\n                    for (InputDevice.MotionRange range : ranges) {\r\n                        if ((range.getSource() & InputDevice.SOURCE_CLASS_JOYSTICK) != 0) {\r\n                            if (range.getAxis() == MotionEvent.AXIS_HAT_X || range.getAxis() == MotionEvent.AXIS_HAT_Y) {\r\n                                joystick.hats.add(range);\r\n                            } else {\r\n                                joystick.axes.add(range);\r\n                            }\r\n                        }\r\n                    }\r\n```\r\n\r\nCurrently in master my Xbox triggers are mapped to [-1;1]. If I remove the duplicate checking functionality, they work just fine (Dualshock 4 triggers too).\r\nMaybe that's also the reason the triggers are swapped in Godot for you?\r\n\r\nThis functionality was added in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/45771 to fix https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/45712 , but to me the original issue looks more like a mapping issue that needs to be checked in SDL testcontroller too, just in case. It also provides a way to setup a mapping for the device, maybe that would be helpful too! Or if it doesn't help, we can leave the duplicate checking functionality only for Nvidia Shield controller.\r\n\r\nI'm gonna add a commit to remove the duplicate checking functionality here. May I ask if you can test your controller with that commit too, please?\r\n\r\nAnd I also just checked and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/56181 was reported only after https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/45771 was merged. It may be a coincidence, or may be not :D","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3888940211/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3945297112","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114338#issuecomment-3945297112","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114338","id":3945297112,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rKHTY","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T15:05:13Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T16:01:34Z","body":"I came up with a way to keep the joypad mapping system backwards-compatible with the old GUID format, see the changes in `core/input/input.cpp`. Basically, if a mapping with the new GUID format wasn't found, the system tries to find one with the old GUID format.\r\n(If both fail, well, the joypad doesn't have a mapping :D)\nI will need to test it later though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3945297112/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4248977244","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114338#issuecomment-4248977244","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114338","id":4248977244,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79Qj9c","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-15T03:55:17Z","updated_at":"2026-04-15T03:55:17Z","body":"I feel like the triggers issues should be fixed in a separate PR since this PR is about the mappings and GUID, but I feel like it should still be easy enough to fix.\nFor now I will need to make the CI pass.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4248977244/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4469558550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114338#issuecomment-4469558550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114338","id":4469558550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCmgNFg","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-17T06:11:23Z","updated_at":"2026-05-17T06:11:23Z","body":"I think it's probably a better idea to integrate SDL joystick for Android later too, instead of merging a fix like this, since we'll need SDL joystick for Android for things like the HIDAPI driver, so I decided to close this PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4469558550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]